lds sold for use in 2014-2018 Toyota Highlander vehicles.  The windshields have an attached wire harness that water may leak into, possibly causing damage to the vehicle's Engine Control Module (ECM).","consequence":"The ECM damage may result in the engine stalling, increasing the risk of a crash.","remedy":"Wanda will notify owners, and service centers will replace the windshields, and inspect the ECM for damage, having it replaced, as necessary, free of charge.  The recall began January 29, 2019.  Owners may contact Wanda customer service at 1-864-281-2760.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":8202,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=18E107000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":6,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2014","make":"TOYOTA","model":"HIGHLANDER"},{"year":"2015","make":"TOYOTA","model":"HIGHLANDER"},{"year":"2016","make":"TOYOTA","model":"HIGHLANDER"},{"year":"9999","make":"WANDA","model":"REPLACEMENT WINDSHIELD"},{"year":"2017","make":"TOYOTA","model":"HIGHLANDER"},{"year":"2018","make":"TOYOTA","model":"HIGHLANDER"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"17V520000","received":"2017-08-23","manufacturer":"Gulf States Toyota, Inc.","component":"EQUIPMENT","summary":"Gulf States Toyota, Inc. (GST) is recalling certain 2017 Toyota Highlander and Highlander Hybrid vehicles equipped with accessory roof rail cross bars.  The fasteners for the roof rails may not be torqued properly.","consequence":"The roof rails may loosen and possibly detach from the vehicle, becoming a road hazard and increasing the risk of a crash.","remedy":"GST will notify owners, and dealers will inspect and properly torque the fasteners, free of charge.  The recall began September 29, 2017.  Owners may contact GST customer service at 1-800-444-1074.  GST's number for this recall is 17R3.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":1121,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=17V520000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":2,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2017","make":"TOYOTA","model":"HIGHLANDER"},{"year":"2017","make":"TOYOTA","model":"HIGHLANDER HYBRID"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"17V295000","received":"2017-05-02","manufacturer":"Gulf States Toyota, Inc.","component":"TIRES:TEMPORARY/EMERGENCY SPARE TIRE","summary":"Gulf States Toyota, Inc. (Gulf States) is recalling certain 2017 4Runner , 86, Avalon, Camry, Camry Hybrid, Corolla, Corolla iM, Highlander, Highlander Hybrid, Prius, Prius C, RAV4, RAV4 Hybrid, Sienna  and Yaris vehicles.  The spare tire air pressure was not adjusted to the proper pressure as stated on the Tire Pressure Label.","consequence":"A spare tire that is not inflated to the proper value may not perform as intended, increasing the risk of a crash.","remedy":"Gulf States will notify owners, and dealers will inspect the spare tires, adjusting their pressure as necessary, free of charge.  The recall began June 15, 2017.  Owners may contact Gulf States customer service at 1-800-444-1074.  Toyota's number for this recall is 17R2.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":409,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=17V295000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":15,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2017","make":"TOYOTA","model":"PRIUS"},{"year":"2017","make":"TOYOTA","model":"SIENNA"},{"year":"2017","make":"TOYOTA","model":"HIGHLANDER"},{"year":"2017","make":"TOYOTA","model":"PRIUS C"},{"year":"2017","make":"TOYOTA","model":"86"},{"year":"2017","make":"TOYOTA","model":"CAMRY"},{"year":"2017","make":